/Alt (Infographic illustrating the relationships between climate variables, fungal species, and toxin production. Aspergillus and aflatoxin are linked to high temperature and dry conditions with peanuts and corn, Fusarium with DON/ZEN and rainfall associated with wheat, OTA with storage systems, and fumonisin-associated maize stress shown overlapping at intermediate conditions. Axes display temperature from hot to cool and moisture from dry to wet, highlighting ecological and post-harvest niches. Symbols represent temperature, rainfall, water activity, and storage moisture.)
