<<
/A 2692 0 R
/Alt (Infographic compares healthy mycobiome, drought-stressed dysbiotic mycobiome, and biocontrol-assisted partial restoration in crop roots using network diagrams. Healthy state shows high diversity, antagonists, and stable interactions. Drought stress causes reduced diversity, weakened suppression, and toxigenic dominance. Biocontrol application partially restores diversity, increases beneficial antagonists, and reduces toxigenic centrality. Legend explains symbols for microbial taxon, interactions, high abundance, and key states.)
/K [25 2693 0 R]
/P 175 0 R
/Pg 56 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (FIGURE 3)
/Type /StructElem
>>
