742 0 obj
<<
/A 2754 0 R
/Alt (Infographic comparing regulatory threshold and biological exposure burden for food contaminants. Left panel illustrates commodities like maize, peanuts, wheat, and cereal grains tested for contaminants, with a pass or fail verdict based on screening limits to identify unsafe items. Right panel shows that consuming multiple below-threshold foods can cumulatively increase exposure, depicted by food items contributing to blood and urine biomarkers in a human figure. Insets highlight mixture burden from various toxins, vulnerability-adjusted exposure for sensitive groups, and how chronic low-dose and mixture exposure over time increases risk, emphasizing host vulnerability.)
/K [34 2755 0 R]
/P 191 0 R
/Pg 58 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (FIGURE 4)
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
